{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005374Z","id":"7dc146d3bb08f33410a61eff90ed540b71fe1ddfe93811df3b2cf865eb6806c9","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'the click's activeTab grant lasts through a reload…' (until() timed out at line 924) failed in a //web:e2e_chrome_overlay run beside the suite's other tests and passed in others, at 4ffb96fbf and at 641706256 alike. Cause recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201: a spurious index.html change event seconds after the watcher's ready makes Vite reload the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":904},"end":{"line":904},"content_hash":"e6467e6f793321e04a45165ca04c2dc6e574bbe3ba2366f27aace2b1d6a45df5"},"summary":"The test at line 904 can fail when Vite fully reloads its page on a late FSEvents report of the copied live site","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005412Z","id":"dbc08752cab5e1c63563fe946eee288eb68793424df45bb647cfec9c8dc10522","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'the panel shows the live page's questions above its threads…' (an AbortError in the panel at the shot on line 1040) failed in a //web:e2e_chrome_overlay run beside the suite's other tests and passed in others, at 4ffb96fbf and at 641706256 alike. Cause recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201: a spurious index.html change event seconds after the watcher's ready makes Vite reload the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":950},"end":{"line":950},"content_hash":"0aab4f4c1625fb094e74399457e1e4d4bfd40903c3b168b126f7b30172177b68"},"summary":"The test at line 950 can fail when Vite fully reloads its page on a late FSEvents report of the copied live site","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005449Z","id":"4f2b9c739610acc423df29dd1ba712597fe75ab2dcfb6080b3196b22ae79294d","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'the panel's Send names the owner's agents…' (seen at 4ffb96fbf) failed in a //web:e2e_chrome_overlay run beside the suite's other tests and passed in others, at 4ffb96fbf and at 641706256 alike. Cause recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201: a spurious index.html change event seconds after the watcher's ready makes Vite reload the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1065},"end":{"line":1065},"content_hash":"d5b40f4777724297ce327f4ce1833d2af0a2e99959e3b597cfc393a80eb96efc"},"summary":"The test at line 1065 can fail when Vite fully reloads its page on a late FSEvents report of the copied live site","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005741Z","id":"3938415e292dbc1b36836608dfe19b64cd2606a91c0b310e9f5af01b54a9053f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"065a23271e08eaba8f879e54ee8156fd3b1139c6a7d14dbcd7874e65743b1bd8","summary":"Reproduced at 4ffb96fbf too (failed in 3 of 7 runs there); the reload comes from a late FSEvents index.html change, recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:28:10.005883Z","id":"69f7b83d096ea73c1e7a51f551640ce0dd052a3bf9ec3c3feea7b8e69483b353","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"83e0a6e0eb997452a9df8e4cdda40d04bb2c8a9ed37c8b715f8722a9a2fbb0a8","summary":"Reproduced at 4ffb96fbf (2 of 7 runs). A trace at 641706256 shows '[vite] hot updated: /main.js' then a full reload during the host's 18 s sleep, with no edit by the test: a late FSEvents report, recorded on web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts:192:201. The click on #save then opened no composer","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:58:08.390852Z","id":"83f3a1237960a431271e0e1abb7a4d5083dbc049725d96a05904c3030195ab00","body":{"detail":"holdOn sends touchStart, waits a fixed 800 ms on the test runner's clock, then touchEnd. The bridge arms on its own page timer (HOLD_MS 450, web/bridge/src/long-press.ts:12, 107-112); under load the page's timer can still be pending when touchEnd arrives, the release is a tap rather than a pick, and 'a long-press picks and Send sends to the app session' fails without a defect. It is also a sleep standing in for a condition, which AGENTS.md's test rules forbid.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"dd47da20ad1f22bad31fe872dac93ab76d36525ba3a891e5374d7d1c34a80d17"},"suggested_fix":"After touchStart, expect.poll in the frame for the armed outline the bridge draws (hooks.armed), then send touchEnd; drop the setTimeout.","summary":"holdOn sleeps 800 ms in place of waiting for the hold to arm","tags":["review","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:50.265056Z","id":"a3a617710057de3d1f921257f4b8808f2cc46590a26e3a75a18fcd40b6b4396c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:daf342ec","summary":"daf342ec: holdOn polls for a new clax:hover with the target's selector (the armed hold's outline) before touchEnd; no fixed wait. npx playwright test e2e/app-mode.spec.ts e2e/long-press.spec.ts e2e/inter-app.spec.ts --repeat-each 3 (3 workers): 54 passed.","supersedes":"83f3a1237960a431271e0e1abb7a4d5083dbc049725d96a05904c3030195ab00","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-questions.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:15:26.324553Z","id":"7a760058b7e8f2135e0aad95f2771f97f6de077f2a545b7315af1e5c15ccaab6","body":{"detail":"The test asks one question, then checks openQuestions({question}) focuses its card. With web/shell/src/app/host.ts focusCard changed to cardOf(null) (always the first card), npx playwright test e2e/app-questions.spec.ts still passes (14 passed with hold-drag.spec.ts); only shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'openQuestions({question}) shows the sheet when that question arrives...' fails. The browser check of the ID path rests on that unit test.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"5baf72fff6a189993384b680851c2d74b7ff164f65af8df0a6fe3fdcb78f7768"},"suggested_fix":"Ask two questions before load and open the second by ID: assert the second card is focused and the first is not.","summary":"openQuestions by ID is exercised with a single open question, so it cannot tell the ID's card from the first card","tags":["review","test-quality","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/drag-release.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:43.657235Z","id":"7bdd372cef80d60ab1b5508d63512235c6762567772bbe75c1023abb0128665d","body":{"detail":"scripts/quality_gates.sh runs `npx playwright install chromium`; inApp skips a test whose engine's executable is missing, so in the gates only the Chromium cases run. Installing webkit in that lane (or a WebKit project in web/playwright.config.ts) would make the WebKit cases gate merges.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"c1c6ec24066092021a1b5eed13874211da1543300acf398a194f92d8dd5904e7"},"summary":"The WebKit cases skip wherever Playwright's WebKit is not installed, which includes the quality gates' e2e lane (it installs Chromium only)","tags":["e2e","webkit","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/db.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329396Z","id":"531fabaa228114adb102fb0aeaef6bb47ea421b7684056bd5b67d944b54c8a22","body":{"detail":"Failure: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest (8 workers) on 2026-10-17, load average 8 to 15: one run failed db-artifact.spec.ts:64 (Allow grants the read), the next user-assets.spec.ts:47 and visibility.spec.ts:34, the next db.spec.ts:52 and user-assets.spec.ts:47, each a 5 s expect timing out (db.spec.ts:65 '\"n\":1' never shown; user-assets.spec.ts:58 name stays '' instead of 'Sam'). bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=-g --test_arg=LAN passed (12.8 s) between them, and an earlier full run at the same code passed. The failing steps wait on a viewer's naming or a grant reaching an open page through the stream, which under load takes longer than the 5 s expect timeout.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"8e486fc52fee90d3498896a2a77892f3bf1713cc6a36b6c3e4bf1433a90edfaa"},"summary":"The LAN-viewer browser tests time out in the full rest project on a loaded machine and pass alone","tags":["flaky","e2e","load","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:10:46.721722Z","id":"7741ba45c2eaee6f3f271aed2bba538063cca33877811bac8b541eede99b8863","body":{"detail":"Failure: expect(view).toHaveText(start) at app-mode.spec.ts:381, Expected \"1:null\", Received \"run-4:{\\\"n\\\":4}\". Seen 2026-10-17 in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest (8 workers) in 3 of 3 full runs with the shell's worker welcome (635cffe69) and in 1 of 2 full runs without it (web/shell/src/stream*.ts checked out from 635cffe69~1), with the same expectation and received text both ways; run alone with --grep and --repeat-each=6 it passed 6 of 6 with the welcome. The test drives the app host's back() and the page's history (claxHost.back, clax:route messages), which the event stream and its worker do not touch. Not diagnosed: the loop reads the latest history message's back flag after each back(), so a stale true from before the last back may let it press back again, or a late one stop it early.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":382},"content_hash":"0191b8a40c018d7e428ddc008ebbe872068955c6ce097dfd6c92c0e1101da492"},"summary":"The app-mode back() test fails in full e2e_rest runs at its last loop: the view stays on the newest route","tags":["e2e","flaky","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:01:23.639879Z","id":"03e1b7273ecd615595b711389c7d3c3e43f2b23d572906eee5602d288819508b","body":{"detail":"shots is join(repo, \"target/flutter-app/home\") with repo resolved from the spec file, which //web:e2e_rest runs from a copy under execroot/_main/_tmp/…/npm-script-*/; the PNGs are discarded with it, and the assertion at :566 (relative(repo, shots) === \"target/flutter-app/home\") pins that path. To look at them, a run must write to a directory named by CLAX_SHOTS_DIR, as web/e2e/app-shots.spec.ts does, which needs that assertion changed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"d07d4a05a3b3f00e9ba1de6b17ba970c1c84de67432fc6dcb053661ba8a66a17"},"summary":"Under Bazel the home renders are written into the test's temporary copy of the tree and lost","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:11:58.615777Z","id":"f5d2c67ce068b22941ddf63e40da4992e5e89e6b5268cfbf4b5c3fc5627c63f1","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §6.2 lists pageWait {waiting} (comment mode or use() waiting on a slow page). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart:638 parses PageWaitMsg and app_screen.dart ignores it, but no file under web/shell/src posts a message of type pageWait (grep -rn pageWait web/shell/src finds only artifact-controller.ts's pageWait.ms timeout). The shell half belongs with the comment-mode work in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-18-professional-ui.md Task 30; once host.ts posts it, add a case here: a page whose use() is held past pageWait.ms posts pageWait true, then false.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":616},"content_hash":"25072385e56532715a4179a8c68c9ba63467391ca2c1d294adb2dafff33e4e5d"},"summary":"The native overlays e2e has no pageWait case: the shell never posts pageWait","tags":["e2e","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:16:28.992297Z","id":"fff869d41c5172f0f917bed2fc4202f41617464d2f73b43cd836a16b94e7fe9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a4a3a3383","summary":"Fixed: 'native overlays › a page slow to parse holds up its use(): the host hears pageWait, then its end' passes (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=app-mode.spec.ts: 41 passed)","supersedes":"f5d2c67ce068b22941ddf63e40da4992e5e89e6b5268cfbf4b5c3fc5627c63f1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:20:14.519198Z","id":"d85879a10c8beae014b719ad602b365ba3f99066f6a8b55f75b0a3eea5053748","body":{"detail":"Ten full runs of bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results on 2026-10-20, with other worktrees' e2e suites running on the same machine. At 944062c4a: 2 of 5 runs failed: once inspect-tests.spec.ts:164 (sandbox journaled migration: 'this document does not exist, or this viewer cannot write it'), once both app-mode.spec.ts:346 (back() loop ended with the view at run-4, line 394) and this test (the Add after naming the viewer at line 249 did not list 'From the LAN', line 250). With web/ reverted to f8c308f7f^ (the six web files of 40dc50c59, 248b51f90, e517b0174 and 97003339f): 2 of 5 failed: questions.spec.ts:129 (a LAN viewer sees no questions) and this test, the same assertion. So neither the lazy artifact handler nor the bridge's part table makes these more likely. Three of the four failing tests turn on the viewer's identity or level just after it changes (this test after PUT /api/viewers/me; inspect-tests.spec.ts:166-167 reads /api/viewers/me from the gallery page and writes data/users/<me>/).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":250},"content_hash":"892f9aa0cd4b4c8389c67a102a0286d892496771471b9543ce049e66376acfee"},"suggested_fix":"Wait for the state the next step needs rather than for the response: after naming the viewer, poll until a write as that viewer is allowed (or the shell reports the new level) before clicking Add; in inspect-tests.spec.ts read the viewer the page's own requests use. For app-mode.spec.ts:393, poll back() after each host back() instead of reading the last history message.","summary":"//web:e2e_rest fails one LAN-viewer or app-mode test in about two runs of five, with or without the app-mode transport's web changes","tags":["review","flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:59:54.678430Z","id":"8526579f79cffe218055afbcac698626d68fbeea0975a92f46ab877c2a9b17a9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ea1b0ae20","summary":"Fixed in ea1b0ae20, a product race: Chromium fired a load at the cross-origin frame for a traversal of the page's own entries, the shell asked the same document to greet again, and app mode's host took that hello for a new document, dropping the page's routes while its last history message still said back: true, so back() did nothing; a route reported while the shell awaited that hello was dropped too. The answer to clax:greet now carries again: true, the host keeps the trail for it, the bridge re-reports its route after that hello, and a new document's hello tells the app when nothing is left to go back to. Evidence: this test alone under --repeat-each=200 with 8 workers failed 8 of 200 before (a diagnostic showed a second clax:hello after the last route), 2 of 200 with the hello fix alone (the dropped route), and passed 400 of 400 after ea1b0ae20; host.test.ts 'history: a load with no new document...' and 'a new document's routes are gone...' failed before and pass.","supersedes":"7741ba45c2eaee6f3f271aed2bba538063cca33877811bac8b541eede99b8863","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:59:55.004657Z","id":"1ed176540176a3d03d77bc49bbf5ba228f7db197750ad19a1ddf2458f4a6f66c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1357fb3e4","summary":"Each failing test's race found and fixed. contract.spec.ts LAN tracker (e50e9231e): the PUT /api/viewers/me answered 409 name_taken, since other tests on the worker's shared daemon give the owner or a person the name Sam; the viewer stayed at the view level (a trace showed both PUTs 409 and the task PUT 404); it now takes a name no other test uses and checks the PUT's 200. app-mode.spec.ts:346 back(): a product race, fixed in ea1b0ae20 (record 7741ba45). questions.spec.ts:129 (1357fb3e4): no route reaches a SharedWorker's requests (a probe's SharedWorker fetch of /api/token got 200 with both page.route and context.route set), and the stream hub's worker asks for the token after a failed connection, making the LAN view the owner; a LAN view now runs the hub in the page. inspect-tests.spec.ts:164 (e0e6ff299): the test's own GET /api/viewers/me could go out before the gallery's token request made the browser the owner and mint a viewer of its own; it now reads the gallery's lookup. After: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results passed 6 of 6 full runs (2026-10-20, other worktrees' suites running), and 740 runs of the three LAN and migration tests natively passed (60 more ended when another build replaced the clax binary).","supersedes":"d85879a10c8beae014b719ad602b365ba3f99066f6a8b55f75b0a3eea5053748","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:25:36.904388Z","id":"f08d17e1b6f18ba9f16c892d2a350571a4027fc91d51a1f3ac28258ca032325e","body":{"detail":"answerScheme fulfils the core's status as it is, so Chromium follows a 3xx (for example the 308 the core answers /v/1/index.html with, to /v/1/). apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt response() (around line 297) answers any 3xx as a 502 whose body says why, since a WebResourceResponse cannot carry one. A browser test that follows a redirect through this stand-in therefore passes where the Android app would show a 502; none in web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts does. Mirroring Android here would make the stand-in stricter than the spec's §4.2 (answer with the frame's status) and than Apple's handler.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":315},"content_hash":"eada481e2f0a9192b4a3515c308d7d6df5b6ecb5eee18a084a65bf5b9c54aa5c"},"summary":"The stand-in scheme passes a 3xx answer through, where Android's WebView answers it as a 502","tags":["app","e2e","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:58:51.840289Z","id":"fda43058c3ccd81a68108326e97560366f730ddb001089f35ff7efc8a9d70911","body":{"detail":"This record says mirroring Android would make the stand-in stricter than Apple's handler. Reply 2dac26a6 (on apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/SchemeHost.kt:269:276) reports a probe of WKWebView on macOS 26.6.2: a 308 with Location handed to WKURLSchemeTask.didReceive is not followed, and WebKit renders the 308's body at the old URL. Neither platform's host can answer a 3xx usefully, so passing it through matches no platform, and every e2e test that follows a redirect (the core answers 308 for /v/<n>, .../index.html and a draft token without its slash: crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:75 and :236, crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs:414) passes here where the app shows a 502 (Android) or a 308 body (Apple). The relay's 3xx rule is the same on both platforms, so it needs no per-platform switch.","kind":"comment","references":"f08d17e1b6f18ba9f16c892d2a350571a4027fc91d51a1f3ac28258ca032325e","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":315},"content_hash":"eada481e2f0a9192b4a3515c308d7d6df5b6ecb5eee18a084a65bf5b9c54aa5c"},"suggested_fix":"In answerScheme, play the answerer's rule from reply 2dac26a6: follow a redirect whose target has the same base inside the core (index.html to ./) and answer the target; answer a document request for /v/<n> with a 200 text/html meta refresh to the Location; any other 3xx becomes 404. Add a test in web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts where a page's <a href=\"index.html\"> and a /v/1 load reach the page, so plan Task 15's lib/core/scheme.dart has an end-to-end twin.","summary":"Apple does not pass a 3xx through either: the stand-in should apply the no-3xx rule of record 2dac26a6 on both platforms, not pass the core's status","tags":["review","e2e","app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:58:51.840965Z","id":"7ff1090ce2e3f45dd49ff2cfec5757ac2e1cd32ec2a9acc578c6a6369790de34","body":{"detail":"committed() returns without switching when no kept navigation matches the committed URL, treating a cross-document commit with no number like a same-document navigation. The previous load then stays this.load: its nonce is still accepted, its calls and streams keep running and pushing into the new document, and loaded() gives the new document claxHost.init (and, with nonceMeta: false, claxTransport.init) under the previous load's nonce. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §4.4 and plan Task 15 say a committed with no number, or one no nonce was minted for, takes none and leaves the load without a channel. A main-frame navigation answered 403, 404 or a non-200 by the core commits this way (answerScheme lines 301-306 mint only for a 200 /a/ answer). The kept number is also replaced only by a 200 shell document, where §4.4's Android pairing replaces it with every isForMainFrame request, so a later main-frame request that answers 404 leaves an earlier navigation's nonce takeable. No test in web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts commits such a load, so plan Task 15 has no e2e twin of the rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"88e50e0cbb578b969281030f8fe4e4db52ee36e2fb528be8116840b11089ceaa"},"suggested_fix":"Tell same-document navigations apart through the CDP session the host already holds (Page.navigatedWithinDocument, or Page.frameNavigated's type), and on any other main-frame commit without a matching kept number call switchTo(null). Number every main-frame request to the shell host in answerScheme and replace kept with it, minting a nonce only for a shell document. Add a test: reload into a 404 artifact and assert the previous load's nonce is dropped and no init runs.","summary":"A main-frame commit the host numbered no nonce for keeps the previous load's channel live, where spec §4.4 leaves such a load without one","tags":["review","e2e","app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:58:51.841186Z","id":"b69ee2eab509e993a3bb7fe1f3975326df6c089ab2fa16083cf4584810868d57","body":{"detail":"With web/shell/src/transport.ts:301-303's `.conn-notice{display:none!important}` replaced in the served /_clax/transport.js by a style that matches nothing (a scratch copy of this spec routing the script through a string replacement), this test passed (1 passed), while the control run of the same scratch copy with no replacement passed too. Nothing in the test makes conn-notice.ts show a notice, so lines 351 and 354 hold whether the app hides notices or not. The parts that fail on a real bug are the subscription count (line 356) and the topics check (line 345). The same scratch copy confirmed that removing host.ts's meta-nonce check on init fails 'an init the app ran for the previous load…' (line 210) and that removing stream-hub.ts's stop on stream_refused 400/403/404 fails 'the stream reopens by the core's end block…' (line 329: 8 streams opened, 7 expected).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"c2914b233e026b94459eff1d91aaeea2c8460583dbd934ef83eef984251c86d3"},"suggested_fix":"Raise a notice the browser would show: hold a call that retrying() makes past STUCK_MS (web/shell/src/lifecycle.ts:89), or answer it 503 with failNext, then assert `.conn-notice` is attached and hidden (toBeAttached plus toBeHidden), so dropping the style fails the test.","summary":"The suspended-WebView test's .conn-notice checks pass with the transport's notice-hiding style removed: no notice is ever raised in it","tags":["review","e2e","test-strength","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:58:51.841220Z","id":"98ec1c27fc24377ff0adac637dd5d217d855cd26df87e17895e81f2bbe704566","body":{"detail":"`h.scheme.filter(...).every(s => s.status === 403)` is true when the probe's fetch of the shell document never reached the scheme. The probe awaits that fetch before it posts, so today the list is non-empty, but nothing pins it; a change that stops the probe's request (a content policy that blocks it first, say) would leave the 403 rule untested while the test still passes.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":391},"end":{"line":392},"content_hash":"8e05d8d34fe11e1080ea7992ee1daa0ee60492726cad5977529da1ffed3b075c"},"suggested_fix":"Take the filtered list, expect its length to be at least 1, then expect every status to be 403.","summary":"The shell-document refusal check holds for an empty list: assert at least one non-main-frame request for /a/ was answered","tags":["review","e2e","test-strength","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:58:51.841261Z","id":"0bbd60377a590ad7900d293d800d68e3e789c55a9d22b08e4203ec3bff707fb4","body":{"detail":"The relay talks to a daemon over HTTP, so its answers differ from the core's in ways plan Task 15 must not copy and app-transport.spec.ts does not notice: (1) callResult headers are the daemon's raw headers (readAll, lines 115-121), including connection, keep-alive, transfer-encoding and date, which the core's oneshot answer through crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs does not carry; (2) streamBlock carries each TCP chunk of the SSE body (line 475), not one hub block per message as spec §2.4 has the core post, so a block can be split or two merged (the shell's reader buffers to the blank line, so tests pass either way); (3) a main-frame navigation to a shell-host path other than /a/ answers 403 (schemeAnswer line 319, `document !== mainNav`), a rule spec §4.2 and plan Task 15 do not state; (4) the refused-path split reads only '?' (line 431) where admit splits on '?' and '#' (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:687). The end blocks themselves match crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs end() and refused() byte for byte, the held-open list matches clax_server::router::held_open plus /api/admin/shutdown, and the not_in_app body matches error_frame_after.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":421},"end":{"line":491},"content_hash":"7c1606261caea5250856b516a39b5c3c7e4116a1e5c71bb1d5d75d85ed1fb8f6"},"suggested_fix":"Drop hop-by-hop headers (connection, keep-alive, transfer-encoding, and content-length, which the transport recomputes) from callResult headers here, and split the SSE body on blank lines before streamBlock, so the stand-in sends what the core sends. Either state the non-/a/ main-frame 403 in spec §4.2 and Task 15's SchemeAnswerer rules or drop it here. Give channel_relay_test.dart a case that a block arrives whole per streamBlock.","summary":"Where the stand-in relay's bytes differ from what plan Task 15's ChannelRelay will send through the core","tags":["review","e2e","app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:42:18.601918Z","id":"b82473bb331b63e694c2a9935bc63d1194696f8899474548db89c165869e0bdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b08bd913e","summary":"Fixed in b08bd913e, as reply fda43058 proposed: answerScheme never fulfils a 3xx. A redirect within the request's origin and directory is followed in the core (at most 5 hops) and answered under the request's URL; a document request for /v/<n> answered 308 is a 200 text/html meta refresh to its Location; any other 3xx is 404 'not found', with the bytes of apps/clax_app/lib/core/scheme.dart. Evidence: app-transport.spec.ts 'the core's redirects never reach the WebView' (an index.html link, a /v/1 load, a non-document /v/1 fetch answered 404, no 3xx in the scheme log) failed with the previous stand-in (Chromium followed the 308 to /v/1/) and passes. Gates on 3223249b8+e64626fb6 (2026-10-20): bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts passed 10 of 10 runs (16 passed each); //web:e2e_rest once: 515 passed, 59 skipped; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:lint pass; //crates/clax-embed:all passes (embed's the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes failed once alongside uncommitted crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs edits of another session and passed rerun alone).","supersedes":"f08d17e1b6f18ba9f16c892d2a350571a4027fc91d51a1f3ac28258ca032325e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:42:18.969395Z","id":"ea2ab02bdd0e20b7c7ffc65b82bec87f64354c6493351655654e0d8e08b79ed1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:de1f6099e","summary":"Fixed in de1f6099e: every main-frame request the answerer gets takes the next number and replaces the kept one (a nonce only for a shell document answered 200); commits come from CDP Page.frameNavigated, same-document navigations from Page.navigatedWithinDocument (no change), and a commit without a matching kept number or with no nonce minted calls switchTo(null). Evidence: app-transport.spec.ts 'a same-document navigation keeps the load's channel; a reload the core answers 404 commits with no nonce and leaves no channel' failed before (h.nonce kept the previous load's) and passes; 0fc73fd8f adds a main-frame /inbox 403 to it. Gates on 3223249b8+e64626fb6 (2026-10-20): bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts passed 10 of 10 runs (16 passed each); //web:e2e_rest once: 515 passed, 59 skipped; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:lint pass; //crates/clax-embed:all passes (embed's the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes failed once alongside uncommitted crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs edits of another session and passed rerun alone).","supersedes":"7ff1090ce2e3f45dd49ff2cfec5757ac2e1cd32ec2a9acc578c6a6369790de34","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:42:19.316516Z","id":"96cb3f06555f19aa4e7b8d8c817ac3579ee82612e53cd1948ed751b40e40ccc5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3ec3a8d41","summary":"Fixed in 3ec3a8d41: 'a call the core holds past the stuck limit raises the shell's notice, which the app's transport hides' opens an artifact the core has none of (no bootstrap), stalls its GET /api/artifacts/<id> past STUCK_MS, and asserts .conn-notice attached with REQUEST_STUCK, not hidden by the shell, hidden by the transport's style, and the call abandoned and asked again. The suspended-WebView test drops the notice checks it could not fail. Evidence: a scratch copy of the spec that removed the transport's .conn-notice style after load failed (toBeHidden: received visible); the committed test passes. Gates on 3223249b8+e64626fb6 (2026-10-20): bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts passed 10 of 10 runs (16 passed each); //web:e2e_rest once: 515 passed, 59 skipped; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:lint pass; //crates/clax-embed:all passes (embed's the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes failed once alongside uncommitted crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs edits of another session and passed rerun alone).","supersedes":"b69ee2eab509e993a3bb7fe1f3975326df6c089ab2fa16083cf4584810868d57","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:42:19.669452Z","id":"67c704560ea7350272fed9b1e995032c43e0c23508ed1b0db2340220852c8bdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:32c370e89","summary":"Fixed in 32c370e89. Taking the list's length showed it was empty: the content policy refuses the probe's fetch of the shell document before it leaves the page, so the 403 rule was never exercised. The test now navigates the content frame itself to the shell document, waits for at least one non-main-frame /a/ request in the scheme log, and expects each answered 403. Evidence: with the length check alone it failed (Received: 0); with the frame's navigation it passes. Gates on 3223249b8+e64626fb6 (2026-10-20): bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts passed 10 of 10 runs (16 passed each); //web:e2e_rest once: 515 passed, 59 skipped; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:lint pass; //crates/clax-embed:all passes (embed's the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes failed once alongside uncommitted crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs edits of another session and passed rerun alone).","supersedes":"98ec1c27fc24377ff0adac637dd5d217d855cd26df87e17895e81f2bbe704566","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:42:20.073659Z","id":"f5ac54651d5a2f1e258b2e2369dadf46654ee54427571b087a6cc67c158d2009","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0fc73fd8f","summary":"Fixed in 0fc73fd8f (shadowing renamed in e64626fb6): readAll drops connection, keep-alive, transfer-encoding and date; streamBlock sends one SSE block per message (SseBlocks); the held-open check splits on '?' and '#'; a main-frame navigation outside /a/ answers Android's native 403 text/plain 'refused', unnumbered, and an unnumbered gallery path the answerer's 403. Spec §4.2 states the main-frame rule; plan Task 15 lists the relay's must-lines. Evidence: in 'calls go out from boot…' the hop-by-hop check failed with the previous stand-in (date in every callResult) and the /api/stream#x call failed with the '?'-only split; the /inbox check failed before (text/plain; charset=utf-8); 'the relay sends one stream message per SSE block' checks SseBlocks on split and merged chunks. All pass. Gates on 3223249b8+e64626fb6 (2026-10-20): bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts passed 10 of 10 runs (16 passed each); //web:e2e_rest once: 515 passed, 59 skipped; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:lint pass; //crates/clax-embed:all passes (embed's the_queue_owner_is_released_when_its_subscriber_goes failed once alongside uncommitted crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs edits of another session and passed rerun alone).","supersedes":"0bbd60377a590ad7900d293d800d68e3e789c55a9d22b08e4203ec3bff707fb4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:48:36.058871Z","id":"b4c69bfc4986b2b8237c14d51948d0314d7bae8c198e46f62505d74aabd23d2c","body":{"detail":"committed() takes kept.nonce when the committed URL is the kept one's; apps/clax_app/lib/core/shell_link.dart ShellLoads keeps a set per navigation number, drops sets up to the committed number, and pins the first candidate the main frame presents. The pin and its dependence on a message before the load event (record 1b459fd9) therefore have no end-to-end check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":417},"content_hash":"9d5e9de0cbdcb239b6173361d31b2b9cc92c5f416f26b9e099919655b2531767"},"suggested_fix":"Play ShellLoads in the stand-in: a Map<number, Set<nonce>>, candidates at the commit, the first presented candidate pins (or the meta read at load, if 1b459fd9's fix is taken), and claxHost.init only after the pin.","summary":"The e2e stand-in's load model is not ShellLoads: it keeps one nonce per number and takes it at the commit, with no set and no pin, so no browser run checks the rule the app's surface uses","tags":["review","task:15","e2e","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-scheme.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:42:33.791609Z","id":"2e047b7c48300d4c969032f4c067cdd33cf3b3b87e2aa8e74a0489f2e8f82d10","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2f022e6c8","summary":"Fixed: the stand-in keeps nonce sets per navigation number, drops sets up to the committed number and pins on the first presented candidate (or the meta read at load), as ShellLoads does. Test: app-transport.spec.ts 'the load is pinned as the app's surface pins it…' (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --nocache_test_results --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=e2e/app-transport.spec.ts: PASSED)","supersedes":"b4c69bfc4986b2b8237c14d51948d0314d7bae8c198e46f62505d74aabd23d2c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
